==Old English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/æaɹx/|lang=ang}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{proto|Germanic|arga-|lang=en}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|ergʰ-|lang=ang}}. Cognate with {{etyl|ofs|-}} {{term|arg|lang=ofs}}, {{etyl|goh|-}} {{term|arg|lang=goh}}, Dutch {{term|erg|lang=nl}}, {{etyl|non|-}} {{term|argr|lang=non}} (Swedish, Danish {{term|arg|lang=sv}}).

====Adjective====
{{infl|ang|adjective}}

# [[cowardly]]

===Etymology 2===
From {{proto|Germanic|arhwō}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|arku-|bow, arrow|lang=ang}}. Near cognates include Gothic {{term|𐌰𐍂𐍈𐌰𐌶𐌽𐌰|tr=arƕazna|lang=got}} and Old Norse {{term|ǫr|lang=non}}; further cognates include Latin {{term|arcus||bow|lang=la}}.

